110:## Findings
114:### SEC-01 — High: inherited PDF parser and conversion dependency exposure
122:Remediation: update and qualify pypdf to a fixed compatible version (scan: 6.21.4+) and address the other seven dependency packages using the precondition table; rebuild images and rerun conversion/worker recovery plus raw dependency scans. Add tested memory/CPU/process isolation for untrusted conversion rather than relying on wall-clock timeout. Preserve PDF magic and offline/remote-fetch restrictions. Owner: AI Engineer + DevOps, with Security verification. Proposed target: 2026-11-10, and before production/untrusted shared conversion exposure. Tracking: SEC-01 in this report / proposed F0026 security carryover.
124:Proposed bounded G4 mitigation: allow only the reviewed local synthetic-fixture feature acceptance; keep current pipeline/writer defaults, no new producer or public/untrusted deployment activation; treat ingestion/conversion dependency remediation and memory containment as explicit preconditions to broader production exposure. F0006 does not introduce or amplify the inherited route. This is a **proposal**, not PM/operator acceptance or a waiver.
